          "path": "_m/d/j/z/4/huguenot-church-wp/huguenot-church-charleston-sc-.jpg",
          "filename": "Huguenot Church, Charleston SC 2016.07.14 (69).jpg",
          "caption": "Charleston, South Carolina's Huguenot Church was built in 1844 and is the only independent Huguenot church in the United States.  The church has been designated a National Historic Landmark and listed on the National Register of Historic Places.  In the late 1600s a flood of Huguenots left France to escape persecution.  Charleston's Huguenot Church included many of these refugees.  Those families remained dominant in the church's affairs long after the initial church was founded.",
          "alt": "Charleston, South Carolina's Huguenot Church was built in 1844 and is the only independent Huguenot church in the United States.  The church has been designated a National Historic Landmark and listed on the National Register of Historic Places.  In the late 1600s a flood of Huguenots left France to escape persecution.  Charleston's Huguenot Church included many of these refugees.  Those families remained dominant in the church's affairs long after the initial church was founded.",
          "width": 3008,
          "height": 1692,
